<ids xmlns="http://standards.buildingsmart.org/IDS" xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://standards.buildingsmart.org/IDS http://standards.buildingsmart.org/IDS/1.0/ids.xsd">
<info>
<title>Example: Primary school renovation and extension - OpenBEP information requirements</title>
<version>Fingerprint C417DBD9D092 · OpenBEP parameter list v0.1</version>
<description>Generated by the OpenBEP Builder. One specification per element type at its target LOD (handover target, or the final design target when no handover target is set). The native Revit model is the contract master; this file only checks IFC exports. Export from Revit with IFC common property sets, base quantities and the OpenBEP user-defined property set file turned on. Where two element types export to the same IFC class (for example building pipes and site utility pipes), an object is checked against both.</description>
<date>2026-10-28</date>
<purpose>BIM uses: Design review / authoring; Visualisation and photometric rendering; 3D coordination / clash avoidance; Cost estimating; Quantity take-off; Handover / record model (COBie-type data); Existing conditions modelling / renovation; Asset register</purpose>
</info>
<specifications>
